federal investigators are looking into  the cause of multiple gas explosions  that erupted in three Massachusetts  towns north of Boston hurricane  Florence's and the blast left dozens of  homes and other buildings demolished or  engulfed in flames one person was killed  and the state's governor says 10 others  were injured crews responded to 70  reports of fires explosions and gas  leaks across Lawrence Andover and North  Andover  Kenneth Craig is in Lawrence where fire  crews have been working throughout the  night  Kenneth good morning well good morning  to you John one of those homes that  exploded is actually right down the  street behind me but to be honest with  you we are being kept pretty far back  because police told me this morning many  of these homes many of these areas are  still being considered active crime  scenes the Andover fire chief described  the scene out here as something like  Armageddon noting that as soon as crews  put out one fire another one would pop  up in the building right next door  flames engulfed more than 60 structures  on Thursday prompting evacuations of  entire neighborhoods and widespread  confusion on roads 18-year old Lionel  Robinson was inside a car right down the  street from where I'm standing when a  chimney from a house explosion fell on  his vehicle he died at the hospital a  few hours later emergency management  officials believe over pressurized gas  lines triggered the fires but  investigators have yet to reveal an  official cause prior to these explosions  the Columbia Gas Company said it would  be upgrading gas lines and neighborhoods  across the state including where the  explosions occurred officials have cut  power to these neighborhoods and they've  shut down the gas lines indefinitely the  Massachusetts governor Charlie Baker  says it could be weeks or even months  kale before we know an official cause of  how this all happened all right can I  thank you very much it looks like a  movie scene when we look a